    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (38 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a **derived, read-only** value on the owner response \u2014 following the exact same pattern already used for other computed fields like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, and `displayName`. Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that derives the value: `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has an email present, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\n```java\n@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n    expression = \"java(owner == null ? null : \"\n        + \"(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\"))\")\n```\n\nSince `normalizeEmail(...)` stores a `null` email when none is supplied, an owner without an email serializes as `\"PHONE\"` and one with an email as `\"EMAIL\"`, satisfying both new tests in `Cp27Tests`.",
